\section{Design principles}{

\enumerate{
\item Biologically grounded — parameters drawn from published dairy science
literature and real sensor platform experience.
\item Pipeline-first — every function accepts the output of the previous
step and adds columns.
\item Education-ready — datasets designed to support teaching statistics,
data wrangling, visualisation, and machine learning.
\item Transparent — all simulation logic is open, documented, and auditable.
\item Interoperable — standard tibbles; works with tidyverse, ggplot2,
caret, tidymodels, and mlr3.
}
}

\section{Reproducibility}{

Every simulation function accepts a \code{seed} argument. Pass the same seed
to reproduce identical datasets across sessions. All outputs carry
\code{synthetic_data = TRUE} so they can never be mistaken for real farm
records.
}

